The '''2021 FA Community Shield''' (also known as '''The FA Community Shield supported by [[McDonald's]]''' for sponsorship reasons) was the 99th [[FA Community Shield]], an annual football match played between the winners of the previous season's [[2020–21 Premier League|Premier League]], [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]], and the winners of the previous season's [[2020–21 FA Cup|FA Cup]], [[Leicester City F.C.|Leicester City]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.manchestereveningnews.co.uk/sport/football/football-news/man-city-leicester-community-shield-20607175|title=Leicester City to face Man City in Community Shield following FA Cup triumph|last=Murphy|first=Daniel|website=Manchester Evening News|date=15 May 2021|access-date=31 July 2021}}</ref> This was Manchester City's first FA Community Shield appearance since [[2019 FA Community Shield|2019]] when they beat [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] 5–4 on [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]] after a 1–1 draw, and Leicester's first since losing 2–1 to [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] in the [[2016 FA Community Shield|2016 edition]]. The game was played on 7 August 2021 at [[Wembley Stadium]] in [[Wembley]], [[London]], with Leicester beating Manchester City 1–0 with a 89th-minute penalty by [[Kelechi Iheanacho]].<ref>{{cite web|title=FA Community Shield: late Iheanacho penalty hands Leicester victory over Man City|url=https://www.thefa.com/news/2021/aug/07/fa-community-shield-report-07082021|website=TheFA.com |publisher=The Football Association|date=7 August 2021|access-date=7 August 2021}}</ref>

[[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] were the holders having won the [[2020 FA Community Shield|2020 edition]], but did not qualify for this match, as they finished eighth in the [[2020–21 Premier League|Premier League]] and were knocked out of the [[2020–21 FA Cup|FA Cup]] in the fourth round. The match was televised live on [[ITV (TV channel)|ITV]]. It was the first time the FA Community Shield went [[free-to-air]] on television since the [[2012 FA Community Shield]], which was also shown on ITV.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/57345116 |title=Community Shield: Man City v Leicester City on 7 August |publisher=BBC |date=3 June 2021 |access-date=16 July 2021}}</ref>

==Background== 
{{Main|2020–21 Leicester City F.C. season|2020–21 Manchester City F.C. season}} 
Leicester City won their first FA Cup title after beating [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] 1–0 in the [[2021 FA Cup final|final]].<ref>{{cite news|first=Phil |last=McNulty|title=Chelsea 0–1 Leicester: Foxes lift FA Cup for first time after Youri Tielemans stunner|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/57055571 |work=BBC Sport|date=15 May 2021|access-date=15 May 2021}}</ref> They were appearing in their third FA Community Shield match, having won one ([[1971 FA Charity Shield|1971]]), and lost one ([[2016 FA Community Shield|2016]]).

Manchester City won their third [[List of English football champions|Premier League title]] in four years under the management of [[Pep Guardiola]], after [[Manchester derby|derby rivals]] [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] lost 2–1 to Leicester at [[Old Trafford]] on 11 May 2021.<ref>{{cite news| first=Simon|last=Stone|title=Man City Premier League champions as Leicester City beat Manchester United|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/56990159 |work=BBC Sport|date=11 May 2021|access-date=11 May 2021}}</ref> They were appearing in their 13th match, having won six ([[1937 FA Charity Shield|1937]], [[1968 FA Charity Shield|1968]], [[1972 FA Charity Shield|1972]], [[2012 FA Community Shield|2012]], [[2018 FA Community Shield|2018]], [[2019 FA Community Shield|2019]]), and lost six ([[1934 FA Charity Shield|1934]], [[1956 FA Charity Shield|1956]], [[1969 FA Charity Shield|1969]], [[1973 FA Charity Shield|1973]], [[2011 FA Community Shield|2011]], [[2014 FA Community Shield|2014]]).

==Match==
===Summary===
In the first half, Steffen managed to save a shot from Vardy with his trailing right foot while diving to the left, with ball coming back off the left post. In the last minute of the match Leicester were awarded a penalty when Aké tripped former City forward [[Kelechi Iheanacho]] in the penalty area after he had failed to control a pass from [[Rodri (footballer, born 1996)|Rodri]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/leicester-man-city-live-stream-community-shield-b1898790.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210807143141/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/leicester-man-city-live-stream-community-shield-b1898790.html |archive-date=2021-08-07 |url-access=limited |url-status=live|title=Leicester vs Man City LIVE: Community Shield result, final score and reaction today|date=7 August 2021|work=The Independent|accessdate= 10 August 2021}}</ref> Iheanacho scored the penalty left-footed to the right of the net to win the game 1–0.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/aug/07/leicester-manchester-city-community-shield-match-report|title=Iheanacho punishes wasteful City to win Community Shield for Leicester|date=7 August 2021|work=Guardian|accessdate= 10 August 2021}}</ref> This was the first time that a team from outside the so-called [[Premier League#Emergence of the "Big Six" (2010s)|Big Six]] had won the Charity/Community Shield since [[1995 FA Charity Shield|1995]], when [[Everton F.C.|Everton]] beat [[Blackburn Rovers F.C.|Blackburn Rovers]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.worldfootball.net/competition/co39/records-winners-list/|title=List of FA Community Shield Winners|date=7 August 2021|work=www.worldfootball.net|access-date= 24 March 2022}}</ref>

