==Post-match==
Leicester City boss [[Brendan Rodgers]] spoke to [[BBC Radio Leicester]] about winning the Community Shield for the first time: "There was a great feeling coming here today. Every Leicester player, fan, staff member coming here, it was a really special feeling. We wanted to take that into the game and keep that feeling going, and thankfully we've done that." [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] manager [[Pep Guardiola]] congratulated Leicester on their win and said, "I am more than satisfied with how we played. Many things were really good, the young players were excellent. We got minutes for players so in general, many good things." Guardiola gave debuts to [[Manchester City F.C. EDS and Academy|academy]] players [[Cole Palmer]], [[Samuel Edozie]] and [[Ben Knight (footballer)|Ben Knight]]; Edozie and Palmer started the match and Knight came off the bench to replace [[Ferran Torres]] in the 74th minute.<ref name="lineups"/>

Leicester City started their [[2021–22 Premier League]] campaign with a 1–0 win over [[Wolverhampton Wanderers F.C.|Wolverhampton Wanderers]] at the [[King Power Stadium]], with [[Jamie Vardy]] scoring the only goal in the 41st minute,<ref>{{Cite news|title=Vardy hands Lage defeat in first game|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/58124900|access-date=18 August 2021}}</ref> while Manchester City began the defence of their league title at the [[Tottenham Hotspur Stadium]] where they faced [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]]; they lost 1–0 to a [[Son Heung-min]] goal in the 55th minute, giving new Tottenham Hotspur head coach [[Nuno Espírito Santo]] his first win in charge of the club. Manchester City's record signing [[Jack Grealish]] made his first start for the club in that match.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Son strike gives Spurs win without Kane|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/58133102|access-date=18 August 2021}}</ref>

